From 11cb9b2ee9274e3cbd4360a89e70261190b053fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Manzano <leftspin@me.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:03:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] screencast: keep an in-flight capture across a pause

Since we drive the graph, entering STREAMING dequeues a buffer and
starts a capture. When the stream pauses before that capture completes
(a GStreamer pipewiresrc consumer does STREAMING, PAUSED, STREAMING
while prerolling), the PAUSED handler queued the buffer to the consumer
unfinished, while the compositor still held the capture frame for it.
Resuming dequeued another buffer and started a second capture. Two
things then go wrong:

- With ext-image-copy-capture, if the first frame is still pending,
  the second create_frame is a duplicate_frame protocol error, which
  ends the Wayland connection.
- The consumer receives the unfinished buffer first, marked corrupted
  and with a zero PTS. GStreamer's basesrc takes a live source's first
  PTS as its time origin, so it then waits until the clock reaches the
  next frame's monotonic PTS (about the machine's uptime), holding the
  buffers, and the stream starves after one frame.

Leave the buffer and its capture alone on pause. The capture queues
the buffer and triggers the next cycle when it completes, and resuming
only starts a capture when no buffer is held.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c | 15 ++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c b/src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c
index 1f24760..4d4d7b2 100644
--- a/src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c
+++ b/src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c
@@ -365,14 +365,15 @@ static void pwr_handle_stream_state_changed(void *data,
 	switch (state) {
 	case PW_STREAM_STATE_STREAMING:
 		cast->pwr_stream_state = true;
-		xdpw_pwr_dequeue_buffer(cast);
-		xdpw_wlr_frame_capture(cast);
-		break;
-	case PW_STREAM_STATE_PAUSED:
-		if (old == PW_STREAM_STATE_STREAMING && cast->current_frame.pw_buffer) {
-			xdpw_pwr_enqueue_buffer(cast);
+		// A capture started before a pause may still be in flight, it will
+		// queue its buffer and trigger the next cycle when it completes
+		if (!cast->current_frame.pw_buffer) {
+			xdpw_pwr_dequeue_buffer(cast);
+			if (cast->current_frame.pw_buffer) {
+				xdpw_wlr_frame_capture(cast);
+			}
 		}
-		// fall through
+		break;
 	default:
 		cast->pwr_stream_state = false;
 		pwr_disarm_process_retry(cast);
